            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-6 mt-4 mt-lg-0">
                <div class="bg-primary text-white rounded-4 p-5 shadow-lg">
                    <h3 class="fw-bold mb-4">Ready to Invoice Your Next Design Project?</h3>

                    <p class="mb-4">
                        Create a professional invoice for your design client in under a minute. No signup, no credit card – just fast, free invoices.
                    </p>

                    <a href="https://ratpdf.com/Invoice/Create" class="btn btn-light btn-lg fw-semibold">
                        Create Design Invoice Now
                    </a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="py-5 bg-light">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="text-center mb-5">
            <h2 class="fw-bold">Frequently Asked Questions for Designers</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="accordion" id="faqAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="faq1">
                    <button class="accordion-button" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse1">
                        What should I include on a design invoice?
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="collapse1" class="accordion-collapse collapse show" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        A design invoice should include your business name/logo, client details, invoice number and date, project name and description (e.g., "Logo design – 3 concepts + 2 rounds of revision"), hourly rate or fixed fee, hours worked (if applicable), any expenses (stock photos, fonts), deposit paid, remaining balance, tax, and payment due date.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="accordion-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="faq2">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse2">
                        Is this design invoice generator really free?
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="collapse2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        Yes! RatPDF's invoice generator is completely free for designers. No hidden fees, subscriptions, or watermarks. Create unlimited invoices and download them as PDF files at no cost.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="accordion-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="faq3">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse3">
                        Can I bill by the hour or fixed project rate?
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="collapse3" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        Absolutely. You can set hourly rates and add quantity (hours) per line item, or use fixed prices for deliverables like "Website home page design – $800". Mix both on the same invoice if needed.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="accordion-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="faq4">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse4">
                        Does it support milestone billing (e.g., 50% upfront, 50% on delivery)?
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="collapse4" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        Yes. You can split the total into milestone line items or use the deposit field to record an upfront payment, with the remaining balance shown automatically. For multi-stage projects, create separate invoices per milestone.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="accordion-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="faq5">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse5">
                        Do I need to create an account to generate invoices?
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="collapse5" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        No account or sign-up is required. Start creating invoices immediately – we don't store any of your data.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="py-5">
    <div class="container text-center">
        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">Create Professional Design Invoices in Seconds</h2>
